{"kind":"reasoning","id":"p10-af06a9e1","text":"Good. Now I have a solid backend picture. Let me look at the frontend pieces: HubsRepsManager (1871 lines — read selectively), RepRegistrationTab, RepAccommodationTab (2818 lines — read selectively), PortalShell, AgcAdminClient + BookingsTab structure, AgcSettingsManager. Also how receipts uploads work (generateReceiptUploadUrl + storage id flow). And `requireRole`/users.ts. And `emails.ts`/templates maybe not needed.

Design decisions before more reading:

**1. Pool top-ups ("add extra rooms to each accommodation")**
Add mutation `addPoolCapacity(sessionToken, poolId, quantity, note)` — increments total, persists override in poolTotals setting (like setPoolTotal), writes ledger entry action "reallocate" with positive delta note "capacity top-up +N", audit log. UI in PoolsTab: each pool card gets an "Add capacity" button opening a small dialog with quantity + note. Also maybe include in listPoolsAdmin a `topUps` count? Keep simple.

**2. POA feature**

Schema:
- New table `agcPoaHubs`: { hubId: id("agcHubs"), enabled: v.boolean(), assignedBy: v.optional(v.string()), createdAt: v.number(), updatedAt: v.number() } index by_hub (unique per hub).
- Extend agcRegistrations and agcBookings with optional `poa` object: `agcPoa = v.object({ status: v.union(v.literal("pending"), v.literal("evidence_submitted"), v.literal("confirmed")), evidenceStorageId: v.optional(v.id("_storage")), evidenceFileName..., evidenceContentType..., evidenceNote: v.optional(v.string()), submittedAt: v.optional(v.numb [… 8,122 characters omitted]  roles include finance? Registration list query allows admin, registration, finance; bookings allows admin, accommodation, finance. A combined POA table ideally lives where both finance sees it. Overview page? I'll create a new tab "Payment on arrival" in AgcAccommodationPage? Hmm — registrations live in /admin/registrations (AgcAdminClient) and accommodation in /admin/accommodation.

Cleanest: add a `poa` tab to BOTH pages? That duplicates component but it's a shared component `PoaTableTab` used in both pages — fine, one component, mounted in both pages. It shows merged table with kind column, and Confirm button (admin/finance). Check AgcAccommodationPage tabs structure (62 lines, easy) and AgcAdminClient (787 lines). Also settings: HubsRepsManager for POA hub assignment — I need to see its structure (1871 lines). Maybe better to put POA assignment in AgcSettingsManager (settings page) — user said "add a feature to the settings where admin can assign hubs". So add a POA section in AgcSettingsManager: list hubs with toggle. Need to see AgcSettingsManager structure.

Also emails: on POA creation, email rep IOU instructions; on confirm, email rep "payment confirmed, receipt now paid". Use queueReviewEmail-like helpers.

Also `listPoaRecordsAdmin` and confirm mutation placement: new module `convex/agcPoa.ts` to keep things tidy. It needs requireRep (agcPortal) for rep queries and requireRole (users).

Check crons/holds: POA bookings have no expiresAt so expire job ignores them (expiresAt undefined → skip). Good.

Excel export: bookings export includes paymentMode — POA bookings will show "payment_on_arrival". Export data feed includes paymentMode; fine. Maybe update src/lib/agcBookingExport label mapping? Check agcBookingExport.ts for payment mode labels. There's a test pinning export shape. I'll add label "Payment on arrival" for the new mode if there's a map.

Reference number prefix: check referenceNumbers.ts.

