All done — implemented, tested, committed, and pushed to GitHub (`master`, commit `e594bfd`).

## What was built

**1. Pool capacity top-ups** — In Accommodation → Pools, every pool card now has an "Add capacity" button. Admins add extra rooms/beds to any accommodation pool; the new total is persisted in the `pool_totals` override (so imports/seeds reproduce it), and a ledger entry + audit log record the change. Backend: `addPoolCapacity` in [agcAdminData.ts](convex/agcAdminData.ts), UI in [PoolsTab.tsx](src/components/admin/agc/PoolsTab.tsx).

**2. Payment on arrival (POA)**
- **Settings → Payment on arrival**: a new section in [AgcSettingsManager.tsx](src/components/admin/agc/AgcSettingsManager.tsx) lists every hub with an instant toggle. Grants are stored in a new `agcPoaHubs` table and **enforced server-side** — `submitPoaRegistration`, `createBooking`, and the Excel booking path all reject non-enrolled hubs, even if the UI is bypassed.
- **Rep portal**: enrolled hubs see "Register — pay on arrival" in [RepRegistrationTab.tsx](src/components/portal/RepRegistrationTab.tsx) and a "Book without paying" toggle in [RepAccommodationTab.tsx](src/components/portal/RepAccommodationTab.tsx) (works for both the manual and Excel flows). POA records are created with `paymentMode: "payment_on_arrival"` and `paymentStatus: "awaiting_payment"` — totals are **never credited** until confirmation.
- **IOU receipts**: generated on demand by the `getPoaIou` query and rendered by [PoaReceiptDialogs.tsx](src/components/portal/PoaReceiptDialogs.tsx) with a print/save-as-PDF view ([agcPoa.ts](src/lib/agcPoa.ts)). **Nothing is stored in the DB** — the receipt is computed from the live record, only becoming a "paid receipt" once the POA status flips to confirmed.
- **Evidence upload**: reps upload payment proof straight from the portal against any POA registration or booking; admins are notified by email and the POA status moves to "evidence submitted".
- **POA status table**: a new "Payment on arrival" tab on the admin registrations console ([PoaTab.tsx](src/components/admin/agc/PoaTab.tsx)), visible to **admin and finance**, covering both registrations and bookings — with filters, evidence links, and a **Confirm payment** action that credits the total, sets paid/confirmed timestamps, confirms booking inventory, emails the rep, and turns the IOU into a paid receipt. Regular review approvals also keep POA state in sync.
- **Rooming**: the room-assignment workflow now accepts POA bookings (beds held until the event deadline), while still gating ordinary unpaid holds — POA guests can be assigned to rooms before payment lands.

## Verification
`convex dev --once` functions ready · `tsc --noEmit` clean · `eslint` clean · **133/133 vitest** (includes new POA tests) · `next build` success. Your push initially conflicted with four newer remote commits (finance dashboard work); I rebased and merged both feature sets, re-ran the full suite, and pushed.

One design note: since finance can't access the accommodation page (area roles), the combined POA table lives on the registrations console, which both admin and finance can reach — it covers registration **and** accommodation records as requested.



