All four items are done and pushed as `09d6953`. Here's what the walk-through turned up.

## 1. Payment-on-arrival comes back with the re-book
`openRebook` now re-ticks the POA option when the hub is still enrolled ([RepAccommodationTab.tsx:2090](src/components/portal/RepAccommodationTab.tsx#L2090)), with a toast line saying so. Walked live as the `adenta` rep: "Book these beds again" on the released `DEVWALK…` hold filled the builder with the same roster (**Mr. Devwalk Dormitory** · Dormitory bed GHS 150 and **Ms. Devwalk Hostel** · Hostel bed GHS 450), the toggle was ticked, and "Reserve & hold" completed the loop — a new booking `HC33984` was created on payment-on-arrival terms with the matching IOU receipt (Dormitory × 1, Hostel × 1). Only the released POA card showed the button; the two expired *offline* bookings correctly showed none.

## 2. Repair history in the Pools tab
[listPoolRepairsAdmin](convex/agcAdminData.ts#L1993) reads the repair's audit trail and the panel renders beside "Recent reallocations". Verified in the browser after pressing the button: `Returned 2 bed(s) from 1 finished booking(s) · devadmin@gmail.com`, then the booking row `DEVWALK-LEAKED ×2 beds expired · devadmin@gmail.com`, and the pool went 996 left / 3 confirmed → 998 left / 1 confirmed. Repair rows now carry the actor, so a manual run reads as the admin and a cron run as "nightly check".

## 3. Nightly repair with a desk alert
`nightlyPoolRepairTick` runs daily at 02:30 UTC: it expires lapsed holds, returns beds held by finished bookings, and only when something moved emails active admin/accommodation/finance users ([alertDeskOfPoolRepair](convex/agcAdminData.ts#L2036)). Tests assert the tick returns the beds, queues exactly one alert per desk user, and stays silent on the next run.

## 4. Browser walk-through findings
The delete guard behaves exactly as asked on both tables — no Actions column, no Delete button until rows are ticked, then the refusal on an all-confirmed selection ("Confirmed registrations cannot be deleted — All 1 selected registration(s) are confirmed — the payment is already credited.", and the accommodation wording), and the mixed selection showing *"…1 selected registration(s) are confirmed and will be kept"* in the confirm dialog, deleting 1 and toasting *"Deleted 1 registration(s) — 1 confirmed registration(s) were kept"*.

**One thing that did not look right, now fixed:** ticking a row's checkbox also opened that row's detail dialog — the row `onClick` fired anyway, because the `stopPropagation` lived inside the `Checkbox`. That made the new selection-only delete flow awkward (a dialog popped up on every tick). The select cell now wraps the checkbox in a click-swallowing container in [data-table.tsx:181](src/components/ui/data-table.tsx#L181); re-tested live: ticking selects with no dialog, while clicking the row body still opens the detail dialog as before.

