The review queue is built, verified, and pushed as **db7811c** (working tree clean, in sync with `origin/master`).

**Where it lives.** The accommodation console has a new **Review flags** tab — [ReviewFlagsTab.tsx](src/components/admin/agc/ReviewFlagsTab.tsx) — reachable from the tab strip and by deep link at `/admin/accommodation?tab=flags` ([AgcAccommodationPage.tsx](src/components/admin/agc/AgcAccommodationPage.tsx#L28), [page.tsx](src/app/admin/(console)/accommodation/page.tsx#L29)). It's gated to the accommodation area, so it's exactly the `admin`/`accommodation` roles who can clear a flag.

**What the reviewer sees.** One row per open flag, newest first, showing what the desk flagged, who raised it *and the role they hold*, the delegate's hub, gender, booking ref and room type, the room and building, payment (Paid / Paid on arrival / raw status), and check-in state — the same reasoning I used on the desk sheet, so a decision doesn't need a trip to another screen. The header strip switches from amber "N records waiting on a review decision" to green "No records are waiting on a review" when the queue is empty. **Review** opens a dialog that repeats the desk's note and record summary, asks for the required outcome note, and clears the flag via the same `resolveCheckinFlag` mutation the desk uses; the row drops off immediately, with a "Show what I cleared" affordance so a session's work is visible without a reload.

**Backend.** `listReviewFlags` ([agcCheckin.ts](convex/agcCheckin.ts#L812)) is approver-only and returns only open flags, resolving each delegate's current room with the flag's snapshot as fallback, so a record that moved after being flagged still reads correctly.

**Verified.** `npx tsc --noEmit` ✓, `npm run lint` ✓ 0 problems (one unescaped apostrophe caught and rephrased), `npx vitest run` **235/235** ✓, `npm run build` ✓. The new test asserts two flags queue newest-first, every carried field (note, raiser, role, hub, room, building, ref, type, payment, check-in state), that the desk role is refused the queue, and that clearing one leaves the other.

One limitation worth naming: the desk's existing review flag was already in the schema and pushed earlier, so nothing here changes the desk's own inline flagging — this only adds the reviewer's screen. And as before I verified by test and build rather than by eye, since the console needs staff credentials; your running dev server will pick the tab up on reload.

A natural next step is letting the reviewer act on the record from this queue, not only clear it — assigning a missing room or authorizing the payment override are the two decisions a flagged record usually needs.
