**Limitations.** Still not clicked through in a browser — the console needs staff credentials and you have a dev server running — so the dialog is covered by tests rather than by eye. The correction dialog opens over the open review dialog, which keeps a half-typed review outcome intact; that stacking is the one piece of behaviour I'd want a human to confirm feels right on screen.

The obvious next step is the authorization question above: let the Accommodation Admin, who works this queue, make the correction themselves rather than routing every wrong name through a super admin.
