Done and pushed as **77f6bb0** on `origin/master` (`32cbbfd..77f6bb0`, working tree clean).

**What's new.** The corrections panel now has a **Team** dropdown beside **Changed by**: *Any team*, then each team with its count (Admin (1), Accommodation (3), …). Picking one answers "what did Accommodation change?" without naming anyone first. The filter runs in [the query](convex/admin.ts#L254) alongside the person and date filters, so it sees the whole ledger rather than only the hundred rows already loaded.

**Making the two filters agree.** A team filter plus a person filter can contradict each other — team "Accommodation" with the person "admin@example.com" matches nothing, and silently returning an empty list would look like a bug. So choosing a team narrows the people offered to that team, and if the person already selected isn't on the newly picked team they're cleared. The person option labels still show the team, so the relationship is visible either way. All three filters combine with AND for the date range, and Clear filters resets all four controls.

**One deliberate boundary.** The team list is built from people who currently hold a role, so a correction by a since-deleted account isn't counted under any team — it still shows under *Anyone* and under that person, labelled "account removed". Inventing a phantom team for it would be worse than the small gap, and I've said so in the code comment.

**Verified.** `npx tsc --noEmit` ✓, `npm run lint` ✓ 0 errors and 0 warnings (I caught and removed one `react-hooks/exhaustive-deps` warning I'd introduced by memoizing over a per-render array — the filter is trivial enough to derive inline), `npx vitest run` **240/240** ✓, `npm run build` ✓. The audit test now also asserts the team counts, each team's rows, a team nobody corrected from returning an empty list, and team-plus-person combining to no match — while `total` and the team list still report the unfiltered picture.

**Limitations.** Unchanged from before: no browser pass (the console needs staff credentials), so the four-control filter bar is verified by tests, types and build rather than by eye — worth a glance to confirm it wraps sensibly at your window width. And team filtering covers the roles that have corrections; a role that has never corrected a delegate won't appear in the dropdown to be filtered down to an empty list.
