Done and pushed as **cb21ad0** on `origin/master` (`40b009a..cb21ad0`, working tree clean).

**What's new.** Inside the desk's *Desk overview & tools* drawer there is now an **Out of service** panel, sitting beside the recent check-ins feed. It lists every room a blocking fault has withdrawn from inventory, each row showing the room name, accommodation type and building, the fault category (Toilet, Water, Electrical, Door/lock, Cleaning), the note in full, and who raised it and when. It reads the same live fault query the row chips use, so it updates the moment a room is flagged or fixed — no refresh, no delegate selected.

**Notes never mistaken for blocks.** Only faults marked "take this room out of inventory" appear as rooms. A passing remark ("needs a sweep") is summarised as a count in the heading — *"· 2 other open faults don't block a room"* — so the desk can tell the difference between a bed it cannot use and a note someone left. When nothing is withdrawn, the panel says so plainly rather than rendering an empty card.

**Getting it fixed.** For roles that can resolve faults (admin, accommodation, room-assignment), a **Fix on the rooms screen** link opens the rooms tab, where the "Mark fixed" action releases the room back into inventory automatically. Check-in staff, who cannot resolve, simply see the list — which is the point: they know which beds to avoid.

**Verified.** `npx tsc --noEmit` ✓, `npx eslint` on the changed file ✓, `npx vitest run` **247/247** ✓, `npm run build` ✓. No browser pass, since the console needs staff credentials and you have your own dev server — the panel's layout is verified by types, lint and build rather than by eye.
