Pushed as **6049a4b** (`8259a15..6049a4b`, clean tree).

**Who can claim a station now.** The server's station registration was admin/accommodation/room-assignment only, which is why a dead-zone desk could queue nothing until someone walked over. A check-in account is now allowed to register a station under two guard rails:

- It must be **posted to that building** — an unposted account is told to ask an admin to post it first, and a posted account can only claim its own building, never another block.
- It may only claim a building whose station **nobody has taken yet**. Once a device is the designated station, a second check-in account cannot steal it; the refusal names the current station and says an admin has to move it. Re-pointing a live station re-routes another desk's queued work, so that stays a deliberate approver action — approvers behave exactly as before.

**First sign-in on the desk.** A posted check-in account whose building has no station now sees a banner under the stat strip: *"Blocks 1–4 has no offline station yet. Claim this device before the connection drops…"* with a **Designate this device** button. It disappears the moment the station exists, and the same action is still available in Desk overview & tools → Offline station. The prompt only shows to check-in staff at their own building, so it does not clutter the central or approver view.

Once claimed, the flow from the previous change takes over with no extra step: check-ins taken offline queue on that device with the **Queued offline** badge, push automatically on reconnect, and dedupe by transaction id. If a queued arrival is pushed before a station exists, the error now points at the designation route instead of telling staff to find an admin.

Both runbooks updated — the in-app offline section and [RUNBOOK-NOV3.md](RUNBOOK-NOV3.md) step 1 now say a posted check-in account can claim its building's station on first sign-in, and that moving one stays with an admin or the room team.

**Checks:** `npx tsc --noEmit` ✓, `npx eslint` on the changed files ✓ (one pre-existing unused `Lock` warning in the runbook, untouched), `npx vitest run` **256/256** across 33 files ✓ — the new test covers the unposted refusal, a posted desk claiming its building, the cross-building refusal, a second desk being blocked from an already-claimed station, and an approver re-pointing it deliberately — `npm run build` ✓. No browser pass; the console needs staff credentials, so the banner and button are verified by types, lint and build rather than by eye.
