Pushed as **ee6065a** (`6049a4b..ee6065a`, clean tree).

**The strip is now a filter bar.** Every delegate tile is a button: tap **Unassigned** and the sheet drops to delegates with no bed; tap **Not arrived** and it drops to everyone still expected; the same for **Checked in**, **Keys issued**, **Keys returned** and **Faulty rooms** (delegates in rooms currently out of inventory). The active tile gets a primary border and ring and reads `aria-pressed`, tapping it again clears the filter, and a **"Showing: Not arrived — N delegates on the sheet"** line with **Show all** appears above the sheet so it is never unclear why rows are missing. The Clear filters button resets it too, and it composes with the existing gender/hub/room-type pills and the search term.

**One real gap had to be closed for Checked out.** The desk query deliberately drops departed delegates, so that tile would have filtered to nothing. `listArrivalDesk` now takes an optional `includeCheckedOut` flag, requested only while that tile is active; departed rows come back with a true `checked_out` status (previously the desk data had no such value) and render as waiting rows — untickable, exactly as before. Every other tile filters the live sheet it already had.

**Two tiles stay read-only, deliberately:** *Reserved rooms* (a reserved room holds no delegates by rule, so there is nothing to filter — the tooltip and hint point at the Reserved rooms panel) and the strip's semantics otherwise stay untouched. Keys tiles filter by the delegate's room key state, and the line above the sheet says so, since one key can cover several delegates.

The runbook's desk section now explains that the delegate tiles are filters and the room tiles are not.

**Checks:** `npx tsc --noEmit` ✓, `npx eslint` on the changed files ✓, `npx vitest run` **256/256** across 33 files ✓ — the check-in test now also proves departed delegates leave the default desk sheet and return with `checked_out` status when `includeCheckedOut` is requested — `npm run build` ✓. No browser pass; the console needs staff credentials, so the tile states and filtering are verified by types, lint and build rather than by eye.
