Pushed as **6eb08d1** (`ee6065a..6eb08d1`, clean tree).

**Offline panel.** The bare count is now a reviewable list: the panel names every delegate the device is holding, with their room, the time the arrival was taken, and their position in the send order. The header still carries **Push and sync** (or *Queued — send when online*), and a line underneath says plainly that nothing on the list has reached the server yet and it sends in that order. The list scrolls inside itself so a long queue cannot push the rest of the desk tools down the page, and it labels the building when a queued entry belongs somewhere other than the desk's current location.

**Desk sheet.** Queued rows now read **“Queued offline 09:42”** instead of just the words, with a hover title naming the delegate and the exact time — so a shift change can see when the arrival was actually taken, not only that it is local. The **Local** badge and the existing guards are unchanged: queued delegates stay untickable for bulk check-in, cannot be checked in a second time from the card, and the card still explains the arrival will send when the station reconnects.

To make the list useful, queue entries now also record the delegate's room alongside name, building and the staff identity — old entries without a room still display fine, they just omit that part of the line.

