**Done — the rule is a nightly cron, not a button.** Payment images now disappear 10 days after finance confirms the payment, and each deletion leaves its own audit row.

## How the rule decides

In [storageMaintenance.ts](convex/storageMaintenance.ts):

- **Only confirmed payments qualify.** Registrations and bookings need `paymentStatus === "confirmed"` (set by the approve decision in finance review); POA images need `poa.status === "confirmed"`. An image attached to an unverified, correction-requested or rejected record is still evidence — it is never touched.
- **The clock starts at confirmation**, using `confirmedAt`, falling back to `paidAt` then `updatedAt` so older rows with partial data still expire instead of lingering forever.
- **The record keeps its facts, loses its photo.** The blob is deleted and `receiptStorageId` / `evidenceStorageId` is cleared so nothing points at a dead file; `receiptFileName`, amount, reference, payment date, method and reviewer all stay. Existing UI already guards on the URL being null, so the "view receipt" link simply stops appearing.
- **One audit entry per file:** action `storage.payment_image_expired`, the record's table and id, actor `system:receipt-retention`, a summary like *Deleted the payment receipt "receipt.webp" for AGC-EXPIRED (0.1 KB) — 10 days after payment was confirmed*, and metadata with the confirmed timestamp, days elapsed, size and retention window.

It runs at **03:15 UTC daily** ([crons.ts](convex/crons.ts)), idempotent — a cleared pointer means a second run finds nothing.

## What admins see

The [storage panel](src/components/admin/StorageMaintenancePanel.tsx) now states the rule in plain language: how many images are waiting, and the date the next one goes — so nobody is surprised when a receipt link disappears.

## Checks

- `npx tsc --noEmit` — clean; `npx eslint` on the changed files — clean.
- New test in [storageOrphans.test.ts](tests/storageOrphans.test.ts) proves the boundary rather than just the happy path: a receipt confirmed 11 days ago and POA evidence confirmed 11 days ago are deleted with pointers cleared and exactly two audit entries naming the right records; a receipt confirmed 3 days ago and one still awaiting verification both survive with their pointers intact; the report shows 1 image queued and the correct next-expiry date. Full suite: **34 files / 261 tests passing**.

## Blocked by your connection

Same as last turn — this machine has no outbound DNS (`Could not resolve host: github.com`), so:

1. **Two commits are local only:** `bd85e9e` (orphan sweep) and `c001d54` (this rule). Run `git push origin master`.
2. **Neither is deployed.** The cron won't exist until `npx convex dev` (and prod via `npx convex deploy`) runs with network — until then nothing is being deleted on either deployment.

One consequence worth flagging: once deployed, the first nightly run will retroactively delete *every* confirmed payment image older than 10 days, which on a live conference could be most of the archive in one pass. If you'd rather see the list before it goes, deploy with the cron commented out, check the panel's "waiting" count and audit log for a day, then enable it.
