Walked it at 390px with the Dev Admin session, and it found a real bug.

## What the sheet does now (verified)

- **Opens from the bar**: tapping "Choose room" mounts the bottom sheet at 717px (85dvh cap), top at 167 on an 844px screen, dimmed backdrop, grab handle, "Choose a room" title and close X.
- **Room list renders and scrolls**: 375 room buttons in the unfiltered view, `scrollHeight` 21,572 vs `clientHeight` 608 — the list scrolls inside the sheet while the header stays put.
- **Picking a room closes the sheet and updates the bar** in one motion: bar read "No delegates ticked · 1 / 1 free bed in 1", button became a disabled "Assign 0", and a "Change room" link appeared to reopen the picker.
- **Filters follow through**: setting the panel's room type to Hostel narrowed the sheet from ~375 rooms to exactly **350, every one Hostel (Blocks 1–8)**, and released the previously chosen room so the bar reset to "Pick a room to assign them to" — the release-on-filter behaviour works as designed.
- **Closes** via the close X and via the backdrop.

## The bug it caught

The assign bar is fixed to the viewport, but the `pb-28` that keeps content clear of it was on the **panel**, not the page. The room groups render *after* the panel, so at the bottom of the page each room card's Assign/Reserve/Edit/Flag issue buttons sat underneath the 91px bar. Moved the padding to the rooms page root in [RoomsTab.tsx](src/components/admin/agc/RoomsTab.tsx#L897-L900); the panel no longer carries it.

Also fixed while there: the panel's own filter triggers said "all", "all" — now "Hub: Any" / "Room type: Any", matching the desk page.

## Two things I could not exercise

- **Ticking a delegate.** This dataset has **0 unassigned delegates** (`Unassigned delegates (0)`), so the count-in-the-bar and the "Assign N" path couldn't be driven without inventing a delegate in your dev data. The tick handler is the same `toggle` the desktop picker uses; only the bar's rendering of `picks.length` is new.
- **Animations in the harness.** After I closed the Next.js dev-tools overlay, the preview tab stopped producing frames (`document.timeline.currentTime` froze, `requestAnimationFrame` never fired), so the sheet sat at `opacity: 0` even though it was open and 717px tall. That's the automation tab, not the app — the first pass rendered it normally and the shared `Sheet` primitive is the same one [RecordDetailSheet](src/components/admin/RecordDetailSheet.tsx) uses in production.

Checks: `tsc --noEmit` clean, eslint clean, `agcPhase2` + `agcRoomOps` 27/27. Committed and pushed as `e89bb2c`.
