Done and pushed as `06e1664`.

## What changed

The assign card was permanent furniture, so the delegate list only ever got two-thirds of the page. It now appears on a condition — `pickerActive` in [BulkAssignPanel.tsx](src/components/admin/agc/BulkAssignPanel.tsx):

- a gender pill other than Any, a hub filter, a room-type filter, or a name search, **or**
- at least one delegate ticked.

Until then the panel renders as `grid-cols-1` — the delegate list owns the full width, exactly like the arrival desk before a delegate is chosen. The same flag gates both presentations, so desktop gets the 340px card and phones get the fixed bar plus the sheet, and neither shows when there's no decision in play.

## Verified live at 1280px and 390px

| State | Grid | Assign UI |
|---|---|---|
| No filter, nothing ticked | `grid-cols-1`, list **943px** | heading not in DOM at all |
| Gender → Male | `lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_340px]`, list **587px** | card visible, **340px** |
| Back to Any | `grid-cols-1` | card removed from DOM |
| Phone, no filter | — | no fixed bar |
| Phone, gender → Male | — | bar appears: "No delegates ticked · Pick a room to assign them to · Choose room" |
| Phone, back to Any | — | bar removed |

Checks: `tsc --noEmit` clean, eslint clean, `agcPhase2` + `agcRoomOps` 27/27 passing.

Two notes: the tick-driven path can't be exercised on this dataset because there are **0 unassigned delegates**, so the `picks.length > 0` branch is verified only by reading the state expression; and the phone page keeps its 112px bottom padding when the bar is hidden, which leaves a little dead scroll space at the very end.
