Done and pushed as `5539b0f`.

## How it works

The padding couldn't just be dropped: when the bar *is* showing, the page must end above it or the last room card's Assign/Edit buttons sit underneath. So the state had to travel one level up.

- [BulkAssignPanel](src/components/admin/agc/BulkAssignPanel.tsx) takes an optional `onPickerActiveChange` and reports its `pickerActive` flag in an effect — the same condition that decides whether the card/bar renders, so the two can't disagree.
- [RoomsTab](src/components/admin/agc/RoomsTab.tsx) holds `assignBarActive` and applies `max-lg:pb-28` only while it's true. Desktop is untouched (`max-lg:` only).

## Verified at 390px

| State | Bar | Root padding |
|---|---|---|
| No filter, nothing ticked | absent | `0px`, class absent |
| Gender → Male | present | `112px`, `max-lg:pb-28` applied |
| Back to Any | absent | class removed, back to `0px` |

Checks: `tsc --noEmit` clean, eslint clean on both files, `agcPhase2` + `agcRoomOps` 27/27 passing. Working tree clean, remote level with local.

One consequence worth knowing: the padding now flickers in step with the filter state — type a letter into the name filter and the bar (and the spacing) appear together. That's the intended behaviour, but it means the page height shifts when the first filter is applied, which on a phone can move the row you were looking at by the bar's height.
