Done and pushed as `8ba7799`. Here's what changed, in the order the problems came up.

## The long phone list

The delegate list had no ceiling on a phone — one column of every unassigned name. It now pages: **12 rows first**, then a full-width *Show 25 more (N left)* button, and the filter header shows *Showing 12 of 240 — filter or search to narrow*. Changing a filter or typing in search restarts the page automatically, so you never land mid-list. Desktop is untouched: it still renders the whole roster inside its 420px scroll box.

## Sticky filters — the real bug

Making the filter row `sticky` did nothing, and the reason was in the shell, not the page: [AdminShell](src/components/admin/AdminShell.tsx#L477) clipped with `overflow-x-hidden` on both the sidebar wrapper and the inset. `overflow-x: hidden` computes `overflow-y: auto`, so those boxes became scrollports that never scroll — any `sticky` inside them pins to a box that can't move, i.e. it silently does nothing. Switching both to `overflow-x-clip` keeps the same horizontal guard without creating a scrollport.

Measured on the running dev server at 390px and 1280px: the filter block now pins at exactly `top: 64px`, flush under the fixed header, and stays there while rows scroll under it. Its travel ends with the card, so it stays put for the length of the roster, then leaves with it.

Two side effects worth knowing: the same fix revives other sticky elements that were dead — the room-type group headers now pin as you scroll a group, and the arrival desk's table header was set to `top-0`, which would have slid it *under* the fixed header, so I moved it to `top-16`.

## Everything else

- **List, not table:** the assignment roster renders as rows (`<li>`) at every width; the page has no `<table>` at all. Confirmed via the DOM.
- **Hub filters:** options are the hub name on its own, with `All hubs` for no filter — in the assign panel *and* on the arrival desk (`Hub: Any` / `Hub: Cross` are gone).
- **Room cards:** `listRoomsAdmin` now returns `guestName` alongside the assignment, and the card prefers it over the unassigned-roster lookup, so a card reads names even when the delegate isn't in the roster the page holds.

## Checks

`tsc --noEmit` clean, eslint clean on all five files, `agcPhase2` + `agcRoomOps` 27/27 passing, and I read the sticky/pin behaviour off the browser at both widths rather than assuming it.

Two things I could not verify or finish myself: the dev database currently has **0 unassigned delegates** (everything is assigned), so I confirmed the paged list renders 12 rows by construction but never saw a 240-name roster on a phone — worth a glance when real arrivals load. And the `guestName` field needs a Convex deploy to production (`bunx convex deploy`) before the rooms cards stop showing ids on the live site; I didn't push to your prod deployment.

The `overflow-x-clip` fix is a global shell change, so other admin pages with sticky headers may now start pinning where they were previously inert. The two I found are handled, but the pre-arrival and ops report pages are worth a scroll to confirm nothing overlaps the header.
