Pushed as `6d5c19e`.

## Pagination, not "show more"

[BulkAssignPanel](src/components/admin/agc/BulkAssignPanel.tsx) now slices the roster 12 rows per page with a footer of `Prev · Page 2 of 20 · Next`, and the header line reads `Showing 13–24 of 240` instead of a bare count. Two details worth calling out:

- The page number is clamped, not just stored — assigning the last delegate on page 4 shrinks the roster and drops the open page back to the last one that still exists, rather than showing an empty page.
- The breakpoint moved from `max-width: 639px` to `1023px`. The list's own 420px scroll box is dropped at `max-lg`, so tablets were getting an *uncapped* column — the very problem the paging was meant to fix. Both now switch together.

## Room members behind a View button

The inline `<ul>` of names is gone. An occupied card shows a single row — `2 members  👁 View` — that opens a dialog listing every delegate with a Remove action. The dialog stores the **room id**, not a snapshot of the room, so a removal re-renders it from the live query instead of leaving a ghost row.

Building that surfaced a small bug in my own first pass: clearing the id on close emptied the lookup during the exit animation, so the dialog flickered "This room is no longer in the inventory" on every close. Open state is now separate from which room is shown; I confirmed the exit frame still reads `C10R1 — members` with the correct count.

## Two cards per phone row

The room grid is `grid-cols-2` at every width below `xl`. At 158px of card width the six action buttons stacked into six rows (198px of a 282px card), so below `sm` they collapse to icon-only with `aria-label`/`title` (`Assign delegates to C10R1`, `History for C10R1`, …) and the labels come back at `sm` and up. Measured at 390px: card height 282px → 146px (183px with a member row), no element spilling past its card, no horizontal scroll on the grid or the page. Desktop is unchanged at 3 × 383px with full labels.

## Checks

`tsc --noEmit` clean, eslint clean, `agcPhase2` + `agcRoomOps` 27/27 passing. In the browser at 390px I verified the 2-up grid geometry, the member row and its dialog (title, both names, 340px wide inside a 390px viewport), and desktop labels returning.

What I could not exercise: the dev database has **0 unassigned delegates**, so the pager's markup never rendered — the slicing is straightforward and type-checked, but no page 2 of 20 was ever clicked. I also didn't run a Remove through to the mutation (it would have re-shuffled your seeded assignments); the live-update path is structural, not observed. One unrelated thing I noticed: the rooms tab renders all 501 cards at once, which is why evaluations kept hitting the 10-second limit — if the page feels heavy on a phone, that's the next thing to fix.
