Pushed as `57ab89e`, on top of the tours rebuild (`6a4bf12`).

## Preferred Hotels

[PreferredHotels](src/components/tours/PreferredHotels.tsx) was 22 hotels rendered as identical white cards with four label/`Separator`/value blocks stacked vertically — around 300px each, one flat column, and no way to find the town you're staying in. It's now:

- **Cards with a hierarchy.** The rate is the focal element, parsed so "GHS 700 per room" renders as a gold `GHS 700` with `per room` beneath it (unparseable rates fall back to the exact text, nothing invented). Hotel name sits in the display serif opposite it, with a warm `card → muted` gradient and a gold hairline across the top, so they're no longer plain white rectangles.
- **Facts as pills, not rows.** Location and capacity are compact chips with icons (`Aburi`, `3 double rooms · 6 double spaces…`) instead of two full separated sections; contact and any discount code sit below, the code as a dashed gold chip.
- **Three across on desktop**, two on tablet, one on phone — **204px per card** at 1280px wide versus ~300px stacked, and no horizontal overflow at 390px.
- **Town filter chips** built from the data, most-stocked first: `All stays 22 · Aburi 6 · Akropong 4 · Peduase 3 · Adukroam 2 · Ahwerase 2 · Obosomaase 2 · Berekusu 1 · Kitase 1 · Mampong 1`. Picking Aburi drops the list to those 6.
- The section header now uses the same eyebrow / ornament / display-title treatment as the rest of the site instead of a lone indigo heading.

## Checks

`tsc --noEmit` and eslint clean (I fixed the one `exhaustive-deps` warning by memoizing the hotel list). `npm run build` passes. In the browser: 22 cards render with the rate, pills and contact line intact; Aburi filter shows exactly 6; desktop grid resolves to three 389px columns with a 16px gap; no horizontal scroll at 390px.

One caveat on method: the preview harness's raw clicks and key presses stopped landing in the page mid-session (no click events reached the document at all), so the filter was verified through the DOM click path, which exercises the same React handler. Scroll-triggered buttons are worth one manual tap on your side.

Both commits are pushed; the dev server is still on `localhost:3000/tours` and registered in the preview panel. Production still needs `npx convex deploy` for the tour schema fields, and the hotels section needs no backend change.
