Pushed as `9e46a8f`.

## Type scale

Bumped the sizes that were carrying real content at 11–12px:

| | Before | Now (mobile → desktop) |
|---|---|---|
| Tour title | 18px | 20px → 24px |
| Tour price | 20px | 24px → 30px |
| Tour facts (time/meals) | 12px | 14px |
| Day / badge chips | 11px | 12px |
| Date rail, step strip, Library note | 11–12px | 14px |
| Hotel name | 20px | 24px |
| Hotel rate | 16px | 20px |
| Hotel pills, contact, filters | 11–12px | 12–14px |

The Select button also moved from `size="sm"` to default and the steppers from 32px to 36px, which matters more on a phone than the type does. Tour rows grew from 199→282px on a 390px screen and 150→169px on desktop; hotels stayed at three 389px columns with no horizontal overflow at either width.

## Receipt upload

The confirmation screen now has an **Upload your payment receipt** card right under the reference number, which is exactly when a guest has the transfer app open:

- Accepts a photo or PDF up to 8 MB, compressed client-side through the existing `compressImageForUpload` (PDFs pass through untouched).
- Uploads to Convex storage, then `tourOrders.attachReceipt` links it to the order — authorised by **reference number *and* the email the booking used**, matched case-insensitively. A reference alone can't touch someone's order; wrong email gets "We could not match that reference number to this email address".
- Validates the **stored blob's real** content type and size from the storage system table, not what the client claims, and only falls back to the declared type when storage records none.
- Replacing a receipt deletes the previous blob. The order stays `pending_payment` — finance still decides.
- Every attach writes an audit entry (`tour.receipt_upload`).

**Admin side:** Admin → Tours → Orders has a new **Receipt** column showing *View* (opening the file in a new tab, without triggering the row click) or *Not uploaded*, the order detail sheet shows "View uploaded receipt", and the CSV export gained a `receipt` column. Tour receipts are also registered as referenced storage, so the orphan sweep you had me build won't delete evidence someone just uploaded.

## Checks

`tsc --noEmit` clean, eslint clean (it caught a `set-state-in-effect` in the portal guard, which I replaced with a hydration-safe `document` check), `npm run build` passes, and **36 test files / 270 tests pass** — including a new [tourReceipts.test.ts](tests/tourReceipts.test.ts) with 7 cases: valid attach, mismatched email refused, unknown reference refused, non-image refused, PDF accepted, blob replaced, and the dashboard list exposing `receiptUrl`. The schema and functions are pushed to your **dev** deployment (`helpful-bass-650`).

Two limits worth stating: I did **not** click the upload through the browser — that needs a real order, and I wasn't willing to leave a junk booking in your dev data — so the UI path is verified by types, build and the tested mutations rather than by an actual file upload. And production still needs `npx convex deploy` for the new fields before guests can upload there.
