## What the cron does

`nightlyOrphanSweepTick` runs daily at 03:45 UTC, 30 minutes after the payment-image retention job. It calls `sweepOrphanedFilesBatch` in up to 4 transactions of 500 files each ([crons.ts](convex/crons.ts)), so one night reclaims up to 2,000 stranded uploads instead of a trickle.

Both the cron and the admin button now share one `sweepOrphans` helper in [storageMaintenance.ts](convex/storageMaintenance.ts), which means the automatic path inherits the exact same safety rules:

- It re-reads every reference table plus all of `_storage` on each batch, so a blob claimed since the last run is never touched.
- The 24h grace window is unchanged — an upload sitting in an open form is safe.
- Each batch writes the same `storage.orphans_swept` audit entry, attributed to `system:storage-sweep` with `automatic: true` and no `actorUserId`, so the log never implies a person pressed something. Failed deletes are counted and never abort the batch.
- The tick stops early once a pass frees nothing, rather than re-scanning three more times.

The Storage panel copy now says uploads are swept overnight and that the button is just for clearing them immediately.

